msgid "ESP8266 wifi telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:19
#: 7af2cccd80df4498a642852c498aa39e
msgid "The ESP8266 wifi module is an inexpensive programmable wifi modules available from many sources.  It also comes included with most :ref:`Pixracers <common-pixracer-overview>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:22
#: 4b5b2509c23d4c4aa4c209a023056eeb
msgid "Where to Buy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:23
#: 85dbe7fa2c6b466e8fe29e8cfb527861
msgid "The `adafruit HUZZAH ESP8266 breakout board <https://www.adafruit.com/product/2471>`__ can be connected to an autopilot without the need for 3.3V regulator or level shifters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:24
#: ad1fb80d46904a1780eaee1030cf80bb
msgid "The `Beyond Robotix - Kahuna <https://www.beyondrobotix.com/products/kahuna>`__ is a ready to use ESP8266 module that connects directly to an autopilot. The Kahuna is pre-flashed with a fork of ArduPilot firmware, has a JST-GH connector to connect easily to several off-the-shelf autopilots and has a u.fl connector for an external antenna. Further documentation for this unit is found `here <https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VyOsp9_q6dIAdYdWuDFcWoqqrNy_vbFMANubZA3Uz5g/edit?usp=sharing>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:25
#: b03665b53eac4214b7e372b1d4027ad1
msgid "`AeroLink:WiFi from Bask Aerospace <https://baskaerospace.com.au/shop/telemetry/aerolink-wifi/>`__ is a ready to use ESP8266 module that connects directly to an autopilot through a Serial Port. The AeroLink:WiFi is pre-flashed with a fork of ArduPilot ESP8266 firmware, has a JST-GH connector to connect easily to several off-the-shelf autopilots and has a built-in antenna. Further documentation the AeroLink:WiFi see the `Manual <https://baskaerospace.com.au/support/manual/aerolink-wifi-user-manual/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:28
#: 2dd1c16f25024782a5ce4ad8cb494b4f
msgid "Connecting to an autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:33
#: 9dbd8cdc33af4c778a124a300d4d1be7
msgid "If connected to Serial1/Telem1 these parameters should be set on the autopilot (if using another telemetry port, replace the \"1\" in the parameter name with the telemetry port's number):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:35
#: 4b4563822c0a4010bf00b69ba8bc555f
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL1_PROTOCOL <SERIAL1_PROTOCOL>` = 2 (MAVLink2) or 1 (MAVLink1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:36
#: 78f6a99c98564ae6b0b4b019f924d55f
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL1_BAUD <SERIAL1_BAUD>` = 921 (921600 baud)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:38
#: 84296e607a5a493c850797beb894d223
msgid "If you have problems connecting, it may help to set :ref:`BRD_SER1_RTSCTS <BRD_SER1_RTSCTS>` = 0 to disable flow control although this is not normally necessary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:41
#: 83c90a810d3e444fa4036dd9b598e3bb
msgid "Connecting from a Ground Station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:43
#: 34ff4a1867454b689c70ec444e11fffe
msgid "load the MAVESP8266 firmware to the device if you haven't already (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:44
#: 7ab6afccd91a4ebe9c48b68bc96c8b30
msgid "on your PC, open the wifi network connections screen and select the wifi access point (SSID \"ArduPilot\" or \"PixRacer\" with a lower case password \"ardupilot\" or \"pixracer\" respectively)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:45
#: c91e3d3b8125449c8cd22e6f3f7f3f66
msgid "on the ground station, set the connection type to UDP and press \"Connect\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:47
#: 585bda1d7b2e44f786198e7242decc0b
msgid "If all is well the ground station will connect, download parameters and the HUD should move as the vehicle is moved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:50
#: d10debc88e984f85874131953eba930b
msgid "Flashing the device with the MAVESP8266 firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:52
#: 93d65355aa09423b8c98c9926ba9eb00
msgid "We recommend flashing the ArduPilot specific version of MAVESP8266 (`binaries <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/MAVESP8266/latest/>`__, `source code <https://github.com/ArduPilot/mavesp8266>`__) over the original `MAVESP8266 <https://github.com/dogmaphobic/mavesp8266>`__ because it includes two additional features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:54
#: bcfcec4318974591a759567b4df7fedd
msgid "mavlink2 support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:55
#: ab74457293cc49b3a655ec4314bd9dcb
msgid "subsequent firmware uploads can be done over wifi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:56
#: 45b13403889746efa74b0f76622837e4
msgid "simple configuration web interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:58
#: c19b6b1f7047419d97b17f33b4f0b166
msgid "An `FTDI Cable like this one from SparkFun <https://www.sparkfun.com/products/9717>`__ is required for at least the first time the firmware is upload to the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:60
#: e6201209458442a68127b4e1d8d2ba90
msgid "If you are using the Adafruit HUZZAH ESP8266 board and are flashing from a Windows PC then you should:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:62
#: f97796b191224dcb9d5657256e61a652
msgid "solder a 6pin header to the narrow end of the board that has the TX, RX, VCC and GND pins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:63
#: cc9fb102923b4a788d3e61a772cb8d22
msgid "connect the device to your computer using the FTDI cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:64
#: 719fa7f4a26749c5b87cbdd35299aeed
msgid "put the device into bootloader mode by pressing both the Reset and GPIO0 buttons, then release the Reset button followed by the GPIO0 button.  the red LED should remain dimly lit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:65
#: da2858469167476f895de10ced75a77c
msgid "download the ArduPilot specific version of MAVESP8266 from `this directory <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/MAVESP8266/latest/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:67
#: 63435ba7cfaf4aa1995a4ec4645a6c35
msgid "`firmware-esp01_1m.bin <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/MAVESP8266/latest/firmware-esp01_1m.bin>`__ is for boards with 1MB of flash (most boards)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:68
#: 4535db5e86e24739be8bf24ab45e8bf0
msgid "`firmware-esp01.bin <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/MAVESP8266/latest/firmware-esp01.bin>`__ is for boards with only 512KB of flash (very old boards)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:69
#: 13b43e8bc67e486a91f9ce36aa068873
msgid "`firmware-esp12e.bin <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/MAVESP8266/latest/firmware-esp12e.bin>`__ is for boards with 4MB of flash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:70
#: 4a614bd6264b43bf8ffd0102c56667f7
msgid "Windows users should download and run the NodeMCU flasher (`64bit <https://github.com/nodemcu/nodemcu-flasher/blob/master/Win64/Release/ESP8266Flasher.exe>`__ or `32bit <https://github.com/nodemcu/nodemcu-flasher/blob/master/Win32/Release/ESP8266Flasher.exe>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:72
#: f2d18b2ca59b4514a865af012c77e10d
msgid "on the Advanced page ensure the Flash size is set to 4MByte"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:73
#: 59f20518dfba41bab6b88ff8c3406911
msgid "on the Config page push the gear and select the firmware downloaded above"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:74
#: e11c0169a0b64e1d9df7cc876af8200b
msgid "on the Operation page select the \"COM Port\" and push the \"Flash\" button.  If successful the blue bar will slowly stretch from left to right and the icon on the bottom left will turn green."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:79
#: 5b9e0de193bd42eb83a6b2ac4462c40d
msgid "Mac users should use the `esptool <https://github.com/espressif/esptool>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:81
#: e131ceb3b5664d318db53dfc8c928c40
msgid "First, find the COM of your connected device by using the following command line in the terminal. The USB COM port that the ESP8266 is attached will appear something  \"/dev/ttyusbserial-A600eto2\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:87
#: 00a2897879fb4d75bc69c97a71477be6
msgid "Next, you need to erase all content in your ESP8266. Put the ESP8266 in bootloader mode, and run this command in your terminal window, replacing the *COM* with the ESP8266 COM port you found previously above"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:93
#: d3ba36e4b1ca413a8cb7c9dc365390e8
msgid "Finally,  flash the board with the correct expected firmware: Put your device in bootloader mode again, and use the following command, again replacing the *COM* with the  port you used in the previous command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:101
#: efe3705feb1648ada403252758658d10
msgid "Linux users should use the `esptool <https://github.com/espressif/esptool>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:104
#: f17a2737284b47b8b094cd5dc60b1a62
msgid "Changing the Wifi SSID and Password"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:106
#: e2ce7045631441b396688bb1ead9e088
msgid "connect from your PC to the wifi access point (initial access point ID is \"ArduPilot\", and password is \"ardupilot\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:107
#: 5d3656a88572404d8391c44319833857
msgid "open a browser to `192.168.4.1 <http://192.168.4.1/>`__ and a simple web interface will appear like below"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:108
#: 7050199e131344188aea39e8c3ba8a9a
msgid "click on the \"Setup\" link"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esp8266-telemetry.rst:109
